#: community-login-idp.php:1653
msgid "Community Login"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1673
msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1675
msgid "Create a new WordPress account when an unknown person signs in"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1676
msgid "Automatically link to an existing account with the same verified email address"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1677
msgid "Only enable automatic linking if you trust the provider to verify email addresses — it lets anyone controlling that email sign in as the matching WordPress user."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1681
msgid "Site visibility"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1683
msgid "Require people to be logged in to view the site"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1684
msgid "Logged-out visitors are sent to the login form. The login form itself, the provider callback, cron and the admin-ajax endpoint stay reachable, as do robots.txt and the favicon."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1687
msgid "Also require login for RSS and Atom feeds"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1688
msgid "Also require login for the REST API"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1690
msgid "Both are off by default because closing them breaks things quietly: feeds stop updating in readers, and a closed REST API stops oEmbed previews of your posts elsewhere along with any theme or plugin that reads the API without a session. Application passwords keep working either way."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1693
msgid "Always allow these paths:"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1696
msgid "One per line, matched as a prefix — /shop covers everything under it. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1700
msgid "Session length"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1703
msgid "hours"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1704
msgid "How long someone stays signed in after using a provider button. Membership of the workspace or server is only rechecked when they sign in again, so this is also how long someone keeps access after leaving your community. The default, 48 hours, matches WordPress’ own."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1708
msgid "Avatars"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1710
msgid "Use the profile picture from the provider"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1711
msgid "Images are hotlinked from Slack’s or Discord’s CDN, which tells them the IP address of every visitor who loads a page with an avatar on it — the same objection people raise about Gravatar. That is why this is off by default. Users with no linked provider, or no picture set there, keep the site’s normal avatar."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1715
msgid "Password sign-in"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1717
msgid "Disable username and password sign-in"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1719
msgid "Interactive logins must then go through a provider above. Application passwords keep working for the REST API and XML-RPC, so integrations are unaffected. Password resets are switched off too, since the resulting password could not be used."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1722
msgid "Before you enable this, link your own account to a provider."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: PHP constant definition to add to wp-config.php.
#: community-login-idp.php:1726
#, php-format
msgid "If a provider ever breaks, restore password sign-in by adding %s to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1739
msgid "Enabled"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1740
msgid "Show a sign-in button for this provider"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1743
msgid "Client ID"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1747
msgid "Client Secret"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1752
msgid "Workspace ID"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1755
msgid "Optional. If set, only members of this Slack workspace may sign in."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1761
msgid "Server ID"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1765
msgid "Optional but strongly recommended. If set, only members of this Discord server may sign in. Leave it empty and any Discord account in the world can register."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1767
msgid "Turn on Developer Mode in Discord, then right-click the server and choose Copy Server ID. Setting this adds the “guilds” permission to the consent screen people see."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1773
msgid "App token"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1786
msgid "Optional. A bot token from the app’s OAuth & Permissions screen. Not needed to sign in — it is for lookups the sign-in flow cannot make, such as whether an account has been deactivated."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1787
msgid "Optional. A bot token from the app’s Bot screen. Not needed to sign in — it is for lookups the sign-in flow cannot make, such as turning role IDs into names."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1791
msgid "It is checked against the provider when you save."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1796
msgid "Role mapping"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1800
msgid "Optional. One rule per line, written as remote role = WordPress role. The first line that matches wins, so put the most privileged one at the top. Anyone matching nothing gets the site’s default role."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1805
msgid "Slack has no roles, so the left-hand side is one of: owner, admin, guest, single_channel_guest, bot, member. Needs the app token above — without it nobody matches."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1806
msgid "The left-hand side is a Discord role ID: turn on Developer Mode, then right-click the role in Server Settings → Roles and choose Copy Role ID. Needs the Server ID above, and adds the “guilds.members.read” permission to the consent screen."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1810
msgid "This applies only when an account is first created."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1811
msgid "Roles are never changed on later sign-ins, so losing a role on the provider does not remove it here — and mapping anything to Administrator hands full control of this site to whoever administers your workspace or server."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1816
msgid "Redirect URL"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1818
msgid "Add this exact URL to the provider app’s allowed redirect URLs."
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1844
msgid "Blocked accounts"
msgstr ""

#: community-login-idp.php:1845
msgid "These remote accounts cannot sign in, whatever else would otherwise let them. Block someone with the row action on the Users screen."
msgstr ""

